QEMU on Windows against MSVC's runtime (WIN_QEMU_CC=msvc, docs/build-windows.md
"QEMU under MSVC"): MSYS2's clang targeting x86_64-pc-windows-msvc, Visual
Studio's headers, the UCRT and the static C runtime, linked by lld-link, against
libraries scripts/build-deps.sh builds for that runtime. Upstream supports only
mingw on Windows; everything here is inert there (host_msvc / _MSC_VER).

- include/msvc/: the POSIX parts of mingw-w64's headers QEMU uses (unistd.h,
  getopt.h, sys/time.h, dirent.h, libgen.h, strings.h; ssize_t, mode_t,
  SSIZE_MAX, O_ACCMODE, S_IRUSR, clock_gettime, mkstemp), on the system include
  path for an MSVC-ABI compiler only. Headers the UCRT also has wrap it with
  #include_next.
- util/oslib-msvc.c: the functions behind them (getopt_long with glibc's
  argument permutation, gettimeofday, clock_gettime, nanosleep, usleep, sleep,
  mkstemp, basename/dirname, opendir over FindFirstFile) and compiler-rt's
  128-bit division (__udivti3 and friends), which clang calls and MSVC's
  libraries lack.
- os-win32.h: setjmp keeps mingw's _setjmp(env, NULL), so longjmp out of TCG's
  generated code never unwinds; MSVC's headers declare _setjmp with one
  parameter, so the UCRT's is called under another name.
- oslib-win32.c: real __try/__except for mingw's __try1/__except1.
- Enums. MSVC's ABI makes every enum an int, whatever its values: an enum in a
  bit-field one bit short of its largest enumerator reads back negative, and an
  enumerator past INT_MAX is truncated (both ABIs' clang agrees; no flag
  changes it). TCGTemp.kind:3 read TEMP_CONST (4) as -4 and TCGOp.opc:8 every
  opcode past 127 as negative (an `la_bb_end: code should not be reached`
  abort), and softfloat's float_status lost its rounding and NaN rules the
  same way. QEMU_ENUM_UNSIGNED(type) (qemu/compiler.h) gives such an enum an
  unsigned underlying type under _MSC_VER and is empty elsewhere: the nine
  bit-field enums, FIELD()/SHARED_FIELD()'s 64-bit masks (about 450 of the
  559 enumerators past INT_MAX), and 26 enums of 32-bit codes with the top
  bit set (rtl8139, net/eth.h, QEMU_ARCH_ALL, Hyper-V's message types, ...).
  The MSVC build makes -Wbitfield-enum-conversion,
  -Wbitfield-constant-conversion and -Wmicrosoft-enum-value errors, so a new
  one fails the build instead of miscompiling.
- vmstate.h: VMSTATE_UINT32_ENUM(_TEST) for four enum fields (sb16, usb-storage,
  xhci, virtio-gpu), which VMSTATE_UINT32's type check refuses as ints; the
  stream is the same four bytes.
- accel-irq.c: an `inline` external definition that clang's MSVC mode emits no
  body for.
- meson.build: host_msvc; lld-link accepted beside ld.lld; _USE_MATH_DEFINES;
  no qemu-nbd (POSIX threads); dxguid for the D-Bus display's DXGI IDs;
  libqemu-embed-*.dll keeps mingw's `lib` prefix, the name the players import.

