diff --git a/include/msvc/README b/include/msvc/README
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d44e90c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/msvc/README
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+POSIX headers for a build against MSVC's runtime (2ksbox patch 83)
+
+QEMU on Windows is written for mingw-w64, whose headers carry the parts
+of POSIX QEMU uses (unistd.h, getopt.h, sys/time.h, dirent.h, ssize_t,
+mode_t, ...). The UCRT and the Windows SDK do not. meson.build puts this
+directory on the system include path when the compiler targets MSVC's
+ABI (it defines _MSC_VER), and nowhere else; the functions behind these
+declarations are util/oslib-msvc.c.
+
+A header the UCRT also has (sys/types.h, sys/stat.h, fcntl.h, time.h)
+includes the UCRT's with #include_next and adds the missing names.
